WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.430 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  November 2014 the worldview 3 satellite  is passing over the vast empty  wilderness of Australia's Northwest Cape  when it captures a huge symbol edged  onto the earth the strangest thing about  this image is its geometric regularity  these lines are very straight the  markings are very clear the shape covers  over one and a half square miles  hexagons a mile wide in the middle of  the desert the site is one of the  furthest points west on the Australian  continent it's miles from anything close  analysis of the image reveals that at  the points of the hexagram there are  thin spike like structures casting long  shadows zooming in on this image we see  a massive array of antennae so the  original pattern we saw was actually  roads connecting all these antennae for  servicing this is no mine the worldview  3 satellite has captured an aerial image  of the most secretive and controversial  military site in Australia a site  established by the US military  it's called base Harold Holt and it's a  u.s. Navy Australian Navy collaboration  they use it to communicate with ships  all over the world  the bass is rumored to operate  top-secret space surveillance systems  developed at White Sands Missile Range  people believe that these hexagon  antennae transmit very low frequency  radio waves these are used among other  things to issue orders to submerged  nuclear submarines extreme low-frequency  e.l.f penetrates into the water because  it's got a long wavelength it's hard to  communicate the submarines  really  and that's an important thing to be able  to talk to your nuclear guys some people  believe that signals from the hexagon  interfered with the controls of a  civilian plane in 2008 forcing it to  make an emergency landing and injuring  over 70 people the incident provoked  speculation that the site could be part  of a secret radio wave weapons program  the International Pilots Association has  called for commercial aircraft to be  barred from the area as a precaution  [Music]  access to the Harold E Holt facility is  highly restricted even today the secrets  of what goes on here remain classified

